<title>USA: Dow climbs 50 points.</title>
<headline>Dow climbs 50 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blue chip stocks jumped in morning trading Wednesday, with the Dow index up more than 50 points as investors were encouraged by a strong bond market.</p>
<p>At 10:10 a.m. EDT, the Dow Jones industrial average was up 51.80. points at 8,226.33, which activated the New York Stock Exchange's limits on program trading. The technology-heavy Nasdaq index gained 6.28 to 1,578.60.</p>
</text>
